course: dictionary
lesson: 819
title: Is it believable?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Believable means easy to believe, or seeming true or possible. A story that could really happen is believable. A story about a flying elephant is not, unless it is a fairy tale and everyone knows that.
explain: Look at the context: «the story she told the teacher was believable, and everyone nodded». The clues are the nods. Everyone agreed it seemed true. Plausibility is a related word in the example «cheek and plausibility such as yours», where plausibility means sounding believable.
explain: Believable can describe a character too. In a story or film, a believable character seems like a real person, with real feelings and real reasons for what they do. You can tell by what they say, what they do and how they change.
explain: Use the word to check claims. When you read news, an advert or a message, ask: is this believable? Scams often try to sound believable, so a believable-sounding message can still be false. The opposite of believable is unbelievable.
fact: Believable means easy to believe, or seeming true or possible.
fact: The opposite of believable is unbelievable.
fact: A believable character seems like a real person in a story or film.
fact: Plausibility means sounding believable.
fact: Scams try to sound believable, so a believable claim is not always a true one.
exercise: «The story she told the teacher was believable, and everyone nodded.» What does believable mean here? | Funny and silly | *Easy to believe and seeming true | Very loud and noisy | Impossible to read
exercise: Which word means the opposite of believable? | quiet | happy | cheap | *unbelievable
exercise: A text says you have won a prize you never entered. Why should you check if it is believable? | Because all texts are true | *Scams can sound believable, so check before you trust it | Because it is a long message | Because prizes are always real
test: «The villain in the film was a believable character, with real fears and real faults.» What does believable tell you about the character? | Cannot talk | *Seems like a real person | Is made of paper | Lives under the sea
test: Tom says he flew to the moon before breakfast. Is his story believable? | Yes, because Tom is clever | Yes, because it is a long story | *No, it is unbelievable, because it is not possible | Yes, it is easy to believe
exam: «The excuse was hardly believable, and the teacher did not believe it.» What does hardly believable mean? | Only just easy to believe | Very heavy | Quite funny | *Very hard to believe
